# Homelab Notes: Moving Proxmox to a New Network

Setup: Proxmox host, Nginx Proxy Manager (NPM), Vaultwarden, TrueNAS VM, Cloudflare DNS, Tailscale.

## Addresses

| Device | Address |
|---|---|
| Router/gateway | 192.168.1.254 |
| Proxmox host | 192.168.1.50 |
| NPM (container 101) | 192.168.1.80 |
| Vaultwarden (container 100) | 192.168.1.82 |
| TrueNAS (VM 104) | 192.168.1.88 |

## 1. Fix Proxmox network (on the host console, as root)

Edit the network config:

```
nano /etc/network/interfaces
```

In the `vmbr0` section:

```
address 192.168.1.50/24
gateway 192.168.1.254
```

Update the hosts file (change only the IP on the host's line):

```
nano /etc/hosts
reboot
```

## 2. Check addresses

```
ip a
pct list
pct exec 100 ip a
pct exec 101 ip a
```

## 3. Tailscale subnet route (remote access)

```
echo 'net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1' >> /etc/sysctl.d/99-tailscale.conf
sysctl -p /etc/sysctl.d/99-tailscale.conf
tailscale up --advertise-routes=192.168.1.0/24
```

Then approve the route in the Tailscale admin console (Machines > Edit route settings).

## 4. Cloudflare DNS (DNS only, private IP, no port forwarding)

```
A      example.com   192.168.1.80          DNS only
CNAME  *             example.com           DNS only
```

## 5. Nginx Proxy Manager hosts

```
nginx.example.com    http://192.168.1.80:81
truenas.example.com  https://192.168.1.88:443
vault.example.com    https://192.168.1.82:8000
```

## 6. Windows hosts file (laptop, PowerShell as Administrator, run once)

```
Add-Content C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts "192.168.1.80 truenas.example.com vault.example.com nginx.example.com"
ipconfig /flushdns
ping vault.example.com
```

Reason: the ISP gateway strips private IPs from DNS answers (rebind protection).

## 7. Tests

```
nslookup vault.example.com 1.1.1.1
nslookup vault.example.com
curl.exe -k --resolve vault.example.com:443:192.168.1.80 https://vault.example.com
```

## 8. Reserve DHCP addresses on the gateway

Reserve 192.168.1.80, 192.168.1.82 and 192.168.1.88 so they don't change.

## Direct addresses (no DNS needed)

```
http://192.168.1.80:81
https://192.168.1.50:8006
https://192.168.1.82:8000
https://192.168.1.88
```

## Troubleshooting notes

- Cloudflare proxied (orange cloud) records can't reach private IPs. Use DNS only.
- Old 192.168.68.x forward addresses in NPM cause 502/504 errors after moving networks.
- The ISP gateway may return no address for names pointing to private IPs.
